---
scope: src/service/buildBrainState
status: aligned
description: Read-only detector that classifies the host's brain wiring state into a closed status vocabulary both runtime probe and brain tool consume identically.
intent: >
  buildBrainState resolves the host project's brain precondition into a
  structured status drawn from a closed vocabulary. It treats the user's
  brain.aide as the source of truth, compares it against the host's MCP
  wiring file, and returns plain data. Unwired slots are recognized by
  shape, never by string content. A config that exists but cannot be read
  or falls short of the required-section contract is reported as invalid
  with its reason, never as absent. The detector is read-only and never throws,
  and performs no path validation, auto-repair, or per-brand dispatch.
outcomes:
  desired:
    - The status vocabulary is closed and uniform — every input (healthy, missing source of truth, outdated or malformed source of truth, missing or unparseable wiring file, content disagreement, structurally unwired slot) collapses into the fixed set of statuses every consumer branches on. The detector never throws; every error and edge case reaches consumers as plain data.
    - The user's brain.aide is the canonical source of truth and is consulted before the wiring file. Disagreement between the two is reported, never silently reconciled, and the wiring file is never treated as authoritative ahead of the user's declaration.
    - Structurally unwired configurations are recognized before content comparison runs, so two equally unwired sides matching each other are surfaced as unwired rather than as healthy agreement.
    - "Detection is pure: brain.aide via the canonical parser, the host's wiring file, and nothing else. No path stat, no writes, no spawned process, no network, no auto-repair on disagreement."
    - The user's brand label is descriptive metadata threaded through unchanged — no code path varies on its value, and detection behavior is identical across brands.
    - A brain config missing required sections reports an outdated status carrying the missing section names, and a present-but-malformed or unreadable one reports what is wrong, carrying the read error when it cannot be read. All stay distinct from the absent-file status, which only a genuinely absent file earns, so the user is told what to fix rather than that the file is missing.
  undesired:
    - Pattern-matching string contents to recognize unwired slots — sentinel strings, angle-bracket markers, magic tokens, or any in-band vocabulary the package would have to keep in sync with templates. Unwired-slot recognition is structural only.
    - Reordering the pipeline so content comparison runs before the structural unwired-slot check, allowing two unwired sides that agree byte-for-byte to surface as healthy.
    - Collapsing an outdated, malformed, or unreadable brain config into the absent-file status, or dropping the parser's or read error's reason on the way through. Unwired slots still map into the existing wiring-not-yet-present status rather than a status of their own.
    - Statting a path, validating a launcher invocation, or otherwise reaching into the user's launch arguments to second-guess them. Path validity is the launcher's problem at server startup.
    - Auto-syncing the wiring file when disagreement is detected, or any other mutation of host files inside this detector. Disagreement is a hard halt the user resolves through the visible sync command.
    - Branching on the user's brand label, importing from any backend registry, or re-implementing brain.aide parsing inline. Format knowledge and brand neutrality are inherited from the parent contract.
---
